
Full linear response calculation for a solute in water.
Standard setup including 500 TIP4P water molecules.
Equilibration = 5M; Averaging = 25M configurations.
Time required: 1.5 hours on a 2.4 GHz Pentium.

If you have a solute Z-matrix and just want to run a standard MC simulation
in TIP4P water, use the xBOX or xBOX725 scripts in boss/scripts

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
xLRCMP is a script to automatically execute an LR job using Z-matrices
from the drugs directory and the OPLS-AA force field with scaled
CM1P charges, e.g., enter

xLRCMP linezo

The linezolid  subdirectory contains output from this command; the directory
was renamed from linezo. If you execute the above command, a directory
named linezo will be created.

This is the most general way to do LR calculations since the OPLS-AA
atom types do not need to be assigned in the Z-matrix. With minor modification
to the xLRCMP script, one could also start from a PDB or mol file rather
than a BOSS Z-matrix; just include execution of the xPDBZ or xMOLZ script.

At the end of the xLRCMP script, the PROPCMP program is executed to estimate
pharmacologically important properties. The key results are in the file propout.
The results are also written to the comma-separated file called csfile. Note:
if csfile does not exist, it is created and includes a header, or if csfile
exists, the results for the current molecule are appended. You could modify
the xLRCMP script so that each time it is executed, the csfile is updated -
please see the xLRCMP script or use the xLRCMPup script. 

One could perform LR calculations for a list of molecules via one job
submission as follows. 
(1) Make a file with the molecule names called "names";
each line has the name of a molecule from the drugs directory like
azt
linezo
etc.
(2) Execute; the results will be summarized in csfile.
xMANY names xLRCMPup
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
xLRCMPhere is a script to automatically execute an LR job using a Z-matrix  
from the current directory and the OPLS-AA force field with scaled
CM1P charges, e.g., enter

xLRCMPhere molecule

The file molecule.z must be in the current directory.

If you wished to start with a mol2 file, e.g., zoloft.mol2, enter
$BOSSdir/scripts/xMOL2Z zoloft   
xLRCMPhere zoloft   

or starting with a PDB file, molecule.pdb, enter
$BOSSdir/scripts/xPDBZ molecule
xLRCMPhere molecule

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
xLRAA is a script to automatically execute an LR job using Z-matrices
from the small directory and the OPLS-AA force field, e.g., enter

xLRAA acmphn

xLR725CMA is a script to automatically execute an LR job using Z-matrices
from the drugs directory, 1.08*CM1A charges, and 725 water molecules, e.g.,
xLR725CMA captop
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

With each script, ADME properties are automatically computed after
the LR job is executed with the PROPCMP or PROPAA programs.
The output is in the propout file. More properties are output with PROPCMP.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

If you just want to run an MC simulation for a solute in water using
the charges as specified in your Z-matrix (OPLS-AA or CMx), then
copy the desired Z-matrix to lrzmat and
csh -e lrcmd >& log &

If appropriate, PROPAA or  PROPCMP could be executed subsequently.

Also, please read the lr.info file.

